STEP 1: Two containers, one IP
------------------------------
vi pod-shared-net.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: shared-net
spec:
  containers:
  - name: web
    image: nginx:1.27
  - name: client
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "sleep 3600"]

k apply -f pod-shared-net.yaml
k get pod shared-net            # READY 2/2
k exec shared-net -c client -- wget -qO- localhost | head -4

The busybox container reached nginx on "localhost": same network
namespace. Note the "-c" flag to choose a container.

k logs shared-net -c web


STEP 2: Sidecar with a shared volume (log shipper pattern)
----------------------------------------------------------
vi pod-sidecar.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: sidecar-demo
spec:
  volumes:
  - name: logs
    emptyDir: {}
  containers:
  - name: app
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "i=0; while true; do echo \"$(date) line $i\" >> /var/log/app.log; i=$((i+1)); sleep 2; done"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: logs
      mountPath: /var/log
  - name: log-shipper
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "tail -F /var/log/app.log"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: logs
      mountPath: /var/log

k apply -f pod-sidecar.yaml
k logs sidecar-demo -c log-shipper -f      # Ctrl+C to stop

The app writes a file; the sidecar reads and prints it.


STEP 3: Init container that waits for a service
-----------------------------------------------
vi pod-init.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: init-demo
spec:
  initContainers:
  - name: wait-for-db
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "until nslookup mydb.default.svc.cluster.local; do echo waiting for mydb; sleep 3; done"]
  - name: prepare
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "echo '<h1>prepared by init</h1>' > /work/index.html"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: html
      mountPath: /work
  containers:
  - name: web
    image: nginx:1.27
    volumeMounts:
    - name: html
      mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
  volumes:
  - name: html
    emptyDir: {}

k apply -f pod-init.yaml
k get pod init-demo               # Init:0/2  (stuck waiting)
k logs init-demo -c wait-for-db   # "waiting for mydb"

Now create the service it is waiting for (you will learn Services in
Week 3; here it is just something for DNS to find):
  k create service clusterip mydb --tcp=5432:5432

k get pod init-demo -w            # Init:1/2 -> PodInitializing -> Running
k exec init-demo -c web -- curl -s localhost


